{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"8.9 x 6 x 1 inches","source_records":["bwb:9781597520829"],"latest_revision":7,"revision":7,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T09:38:13.731961"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-09-29T06:06:13.668928"}}},"ISBN:9781570750410":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781570750410","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL788003M/The_Gospel_of_Mark","preview":"borrow","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/gospelofmarkmahy0000keen","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/818274-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Orbis Books"],"number_of_pages":423,"subtitle":"a Mahāyāna reading","series":["Faith meets faith"],"covers":[818274],"local_id":["urn:cst:10011463182"],"lc_classifications":["BS2585.3 .K44 1995","BS2585.3.K44 1995","BSBS2580.3 .K44 1995","BS2580.3 .K44 1995"],"key":"/books/OL788003M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL446028A","name":"John P. Keenan"}],"publish_places":["Maryknoll, N.Y"],"subjects":["Bible. N.T. Mark -- Commentaries.","Bible. N.T. Mark -- Buddhist interpretations.","Mahayana Buddhism -- Doctrines.","Christianity and other religions -- Mahayana Buddhism.","Mahayana Buddhism -- Relations -- Christianity."],"pagination":"viii, 423 p. ;","source_records":["marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_barcode.mrc:217870875:3492","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part24.utf8:105971417:923","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_multibarcode.mrc:218139910:3492","ia:gospelofmarkmahy0000keen","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-009.mrc:418747541:1401","bwb:9781570750410","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-004.mrc:271323266:2968","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_009.bib.mrc:335449261:2848"],"title":"The Gospel of Mark","dewey_decimal_class":["226.3/077/0882943"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 398-413) and indexes."},"identifiers":{"librarything":["688830"],"goodreads":["948840"]},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lccn":["95020341"],"isbn_10":["1570750416"],"publish_date":"1995","publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"John P. Keenan.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2926634W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"ocaid":"gospelofmarkmahy0000keen","oclc_numbers":["32625597"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Part One of The Gospel of Mark provides an overview of different interpretive techniques in Markan scholarship. It describes and argues for the validity of a Buddhist approach to this \"charter document of the Christian Gospel.\" Here the author demonstrates a profound grasp not only of scriptural scholarship but of Mahayana philosophy.\n\nKeenan discusses themes such as Mark's elliptical style and the \"journeying\" that provides the impetus for the narrative, and explores them through the lens of \"emptiness\" and \"dependent co-arising\" which are the focal points of a Mahayana reading.\n\nIn Part Two Keenan gives the reader truly fresh insights into the paradoxical world of Mark's Jesus. Through a Buddhist lens, the text offers startling and new perspectives on Jesus himself, the experience of the \"Kingdom,\" miracle stories and parables, the passion and death, the resurrection and return."},"latest_revision":13,"revision":13,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-07-25T23:29:35.210701"}}},"ISBN:9780883446409":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780883446409","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL21126116M/The_meaning_of_Christ","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL21126116M/The_meaning_of_Christ","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8559959-S.jpg","details":{"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Bibliogr.\n\n4"},"identifiers":{"librarything":["1278514"],"goodreads":["615993"]},"title":"The meaning of Christ","subtitle":"a Mahayana theology","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL446028A","name":"John P. Keenan"}],"publish_date":"1989","publishers":["Orbis Books"],"series":["Faith meets faith series"],"covers":[8559959],"local_id":["urn:cst:10011329796","urn:scms:0188500174142"],"lc_classifications":["BT205'K43'1989","BT205 .K43 1989"],"publish_places":["Maryknoll, NY"],"subjects":["Jesus Christ -- Person and offices","Jesus Christ -- Buddhist interpretations","Faith.","Enlightenment (Buddhism)","Mysticism.","Christianity and other religions -- Mahayana Buddhism","Mahayana Buddhism -- Relations -- Christianity"],"pagination":"viii, 312 p","source_records":["amazon:0883446405","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_barcode.mrc:176551604:4257","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part19.utf8:115025826:1065","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_multibarcode.mrc:176795548:4257","marc:marc_scms/20220805_ADAM_MARC_records.mrc:86749770:1883","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-009.mrc:486268633:1696","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.01.20150123.full.mrc:773306242:1274","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_008.bib.mrc:307022496:4483"],"lccn":["89037873"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["0883446405"],"publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"John P. Keenan","type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"key":"/books/OL21126116M","number_of_pages":312,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL2926635W"}],"oclc_numbers":["20134075"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The Meaning of Christ reinterprets Christian tradition in the light of Mahāyāna Buddhist philosophy. Mahāyāna theology declares Christ to be \"empty of essence,\" defined only in the \"dependently co-arisen\" course of his life, death, and resurrection. Kenan uses Buddhist thought to unveil \"facets of meaning in Christ not focused on in western thinking,\" and to enable western Christians to reclaim their mystic tradition. Part I examines the meaning of Christ as developed in the early church. Through primary sources, Keenan brings to lifht the cumulative research, interpretations and historical understanding of a broad host of Christian scholars. He argues that the Christian West has failed to relate its own mystic thinkers to its doctrinal, theoretical thinking. Part II outlines Indian Buddhist thought from the early Nikāyas through the Abhidharma theorists, the Prajn̄āpāramitaā and Mādhyanuja thinkers, to the development of critical theory in Yogācāra. Keenan then develops the Yogācāra concept of consciousness, addresses some of the objections to the adoption of Mahāyāna philosophy in Christian theology, and applies the Mahāyāna approach to the doctrines of Incarnation and Trinity."},"latest_revision":13,"revision":13,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-10-31T23:28:19.152936"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-07-12T06:41:29.435973"}}},"ISBN:9780883446416":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780883446416","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL2214781M/The_meaning_of_Christ","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL2214781M/The_meaning_of_Christ","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/680945-S.jpg","details":{"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 295-307) and index."},"identifiers":{"goodreads":["615993"],"librarything":["1278514"]},"title":"The meaning of Christ","subtitle":"a Mahāyāna theology","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL446028A","name":"John P. Keenan"}],"publish_date":"1989","publishers":["Orbis Books"],"isbn_10":["0883446413","0883446405"],"series":["Faith meets faith series","Faith meets faith."],"covers":[680945],"lc_classifications":["BT205 .K43 1989"],"publish_places":["Maryknoll, N.Y"],"pagination":"viii, 312 p. ;","source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part20.dat:157083769:1059","marc:marc_ithaca_college/ic_marc.mrc:46592762:1090","amazon:0883446413","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-07-28"],"dewey_decimal_class":["232"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lccn":["89037873"],"subjects":["Jesus Christ -- Person and offices","Jesus Christ -- Buddhist interpretations","Faith -- Comparative studies","Enlightenment (Buddhism)","Mysticism -- Comparative studies","Christianity and other religions -- Mahāyāna Buddhism","Mahāyāna Buddhism -- Relations -- Christianity"],"publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"John P. Keenan.","type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:O8-BHN-734"],"key":"/books/OL2214781M","number_of_pages":312,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL2926635W"}],"latest_revision":12,"revision":12,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-09-04T03:06:47.624592"}}},"ISBN:9780809141685":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780809141685","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL22621798M/The_wisdom_of_James","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL22621798M/The_wisdom_of_James","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13846185-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["The Newman Press","Newman Press"],"number_of_pages":266,"subtitle":"parallels with Mahāyāna Buddhism","isbn_10":["080914168X"],"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL446028A","name":"John P. Keenan"}],"lc_classifications":["BS2785.52 .K44 2005"],"key":"/books/OL22621798M","publish_places":["New York"],"pagination":"vi, 266 p. ;","title":"The wisdom of James","dewey_decimal_class":["227/.9106"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references (p. 245-261) and index."},"identifiers":{"goodreads":["667358"],"librarything":["4610359"]},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"url":["http://www.loc.gov/catdir/toc/ecip0420/2004016583.html"],"subjects":["Bible. -- N.T. -- James x  Criticism, interpretation, etc.","Mahayana Buddhism."],"publish_date":"2005","publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"John P. Keenan.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2926636W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"lccn":["2004016583"],"source_records":["marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part31.utf8:155531474:811","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-011.mrc:231557671:1708","amazon:080914168X","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2024-01-10:P9-AVX-011","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.09.20150123.full.mrc:590416532:775","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_037.bib.mrc:302259564:1402"],"oclc_numbers":["56011785"],"covers":[13846185],"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:P9-AVX-011"],"latest_revision":10,"revision":10,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-11-17T16:42:09.744626"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-05-10T09:51:28.603157"}}},"ISBN:9780199391349":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780199391349","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28597675M/Training_Anthology_of_Santideva","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL28597675M/Training_Anthology_of_Santideva","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13275888-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Oxford University Press, Incorporated","Oxford University Press","Oxford University Press, USA"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subtitle":"A Translation of the Siksa-Samuccaya","source_records":["bwb:9780199391349","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part42.utf8:97629211:1196","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part42.utf8:101291303:1400","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-026.mrc:121643853:3366","amazon:0199391343","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_026.bib.mrc:27744084:4420"],"title":"Training Anthology of Santideva","lccn":["2015044389","2015047765"],"number_of_pages":520,"isbn_13":["9780199391349"],"lc_classifications":["BQ3242.E5G66 2016","BQ3242.E5 G66 2016","BQ3242.E5"],"publish_date":"2016","key":"/books/OL28597675M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL3507079A","name":"Charles Goodman"}],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL21126735W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"subjects":["Buddhism"],"oclc_numbers":["931226744"],"covers":[13275888],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"The Training Anthology--or Siksa-samuccaya--is a collection of quotations from Buddhist sutras with illuminating and insightful commentary by the eighth-century North Indian master Santideva. Best known for his philosophical poem, the Bodhicaryavatara, Santideva has been a vital source of spiritual guidance and literary inspiration to Tibetan teachers and students throughout the history of Tibetan Buddhism. Charles Goodman offers a translation of this major work of religious literature, in which Santideva has extracted, from the vast ocean of the Buddha's teachings, a large number of passages of exceptional value, either for their practical relevance, philosophical illumination, or aesthetic beauty. It provides a comprehensive overview of the Mahayana path to Awakening and gives scholars an invaluable window into the religious doctrines, ethical commitments, and everyday life of Buddhist monks in India during the first millennium CE.\"--Provided by publisher."},"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-05T03:16:12.391685"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-12-16T02:09:29.274442"}}}}